{"id": "en-f9851472-0001", "text": "The safest bet is one Postgres with daily WAL archiving. Actually, no. A write-heavy ingest path will not survive a failover test, so we shard from the start.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 57, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 28, "topic_id": "db-sharding-plan", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0002", "text": "You can just commit straight to main and push. On second thought, that is reckless on a shared branch. Use a short-lived feature branch and open a PR so the reviewer can see the diff.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 47, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 35, "topic_id": "git-branch-hygiene", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-f9851472-0003", "text": "直接把缓存设成十分钟就够用了。其实不对，写后读一致性会被破坏，更稳妥的是按写入时间戳失效，这样读到的数据与写入顺序一致。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 15, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "strong-phrase", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 60, "topic_id": "cache-ttl-plan", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0004", "text": "We should parse the config with a strict schema so typos fail fast. Wait — that breaks the existing user configs that have extra keys. We need permissive parsing plus a warning log instead.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 68, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 34, "topic_id": "config-parsing", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0005", "text": "Encoding the payload as base64 keeps it text-safe over the wire. Hold on, base64 inflates size by a third and we are already near the MTU; binary framing is the better call here.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 65, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 33, "topic_id": "wire-format", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-f9851472-0006", "text": "先用同步的方式把结果写回主线程就行了。等等，这个界面在大数据量下会卡死，必须放到后台线程里再回调，否则用户会看到界面长时间无响应。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 19, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "interjection", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 65, "topic_id": "threading-ui", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0007", "text": "Pinning the dependency to an exact version makes builds reproducible, which is good. That works, but it silently skips security patches, so a range with a lockfile is safer.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 85, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 29, "topic_id": "dep-versioning", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0008", "text": "Serving static assets from the app server is simpler to deploy. That is fine, but it couples asset scaling to API scaling, and in a traffic spike you want to scale them independently.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 64, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 33, "topic_id": "static-asset-serving", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-f9851472-0009", "text": "用单表存所有订单最省事。这样可以，但一旦数据过亿，分页查询会拖垮整个库，所以还是按月份分表更现实，查询时先定位到对应月份的分片。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 12, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 64, "topic_id": "order-table-partition", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-f9851472-0010", "text": "让前端直接把令牌存在本地存储里实现最简单。这没问题，但一旦脚本注入漏洞得手就能直接偷走凭证，改用仅限服务端读取的会话凭据更安全。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 21, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "clausal-adversative", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 64, "topic_id": "token-storage", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0011", "text": "I said read the file synchronously at startup — that is wrong. It must be async, otherwise a slow disk blocks the whole event loop and every request stalls behind it.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 0, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 31, "topic_id": "startup-file-read", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0012", "text": "Earlier I told you to cache the compiled regexes globally. Let me correct that: global mutable caches leak across tenant requests, so the cache must be scoped per request context.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 59, "scenario": "coding", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 30, "topic_id": "regex-cache-scope", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-f9851472-0013", "text": "我刚才说把日志直接写到控制台就行，其实说错了。生产环境必须写结构化文件，否则容器重启后现场全丢，排障时根本无从下手。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 17, "scenario": "debugging", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 58, "topic_id": "logging-sink", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "zh-f9851472-0014", "text": "前面我建议把整个目录递归删除再重建，这个说法不对。那样会误删用户的本地改动，应该只清理构建产物目录，保留源码和配置文件。", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 18, "scenario": "planning", "turn_type": "self-correction", "is_negative": false, "lang": "zh", "word_count": 60, "topic_id": "clean-rebuild", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0015", "text": "Rewriting the module in Rust would cut latency a lot, and the team seems keen. That seems fine… then again, no Rust experience on the team means the maintenance cost is prohibitive.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 79, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 32, "topic_id": "rust-rewrite", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
{"id": "en-f9851472-0016", "text": "Bumping the thread pool to 64 workers should raise throughput. Looks reasonable at first… on reflection it just moves the bottleneck to the DB connection pool and adds more context-switching.", "has_turn": true, "first_turn_pos": 63, "scenario": "analysis", "turn_type": "hedged-return", "is_negative": false, "lang": "en", "word_count": 30, "topic_id": "threadpool-tuning", "source_model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud", "peer_session": "f9851472-9d8a-4fcc-8c7c-3bbca4d7210b", "provenance": "generated", "conjunction": null, "verified_by": [], "verdict": "pending"}
